  "goodToKnow": "Der Diskurs is discourse: the way a society discusses a topic, as in der öffentliche Diskurs, der gesellschaftliche Diskurs. It's common in academia, media and politics, sometimes criticised as jargon; in everyday speech, Germans say die Debatte or die Diskussion. The philosopher Jürgen Habermas developed the Diskursethik (discourse ethics) and is one of Germany's best-known public intellectuals. Plural: die Diskurse."
